Scripts placed in this directory (*.sql, *.sh, *.sql.gz) run once, in
alphabetical order, the first time the MySQL data volume is initialised.

They run BEFORE the backend has created any tables (Hibernate ddl-auto), so
they can only be used for database/user/charset level setup — not for seeding
application rows.

To seed demo data instead, start the stack, let the backend create the schema,
register the users, then run:

    ./deploy/scripts/seed-demo.sh
